Message-ID: <00c201d0801c$4546eca0$cfd4c5e0$@um.edu.mt>

Hello List,

Thanks for the feedback (on and off list), I have solved the problem.
As it turned out that the output of readbitmap is not easily understood
(at least by me, but I always struggle with data structures in R); the
solution
was to use PNG images as input.

This worked out quite well, with some additional adjustments:

	myImg = readPNG (fileName)   #requires module png

	#some png have a transparency layer, which we get rid of by using
               # the RGB values (i.e., the first three levels on the third
dimension of the matrix) only 
               # for each pixel (i.e., all combinations of levels on the
first two dimensions)

	addToPlot <- as.raster(myImg[ , ,1:3])  

	#now add anywhere on the plot (determined by x1, x2, y1,y2
               rasterImage(addToPlot, x1, x2, y1, y2, interpolate=T)
               
Kind regards,
Holger
 
	

